course: dictionary
lesson: 7570
title: Presenter: one word, more than one job
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A presenter is a person who introduces and hosts a show, or who talks to an audience. You can work out the meaning from the words around it. «A TV weather presenter stands in front of a plain green screen» tells you the presenter is on screen, talking to people who are watching.
explain: Look for clues. «Breakfast-show presenters are paid professionals working from a running order» tells you the job is planned and the presenter is paid to do it. Swap in your meaning: "paid professionals who host the show" still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
explain: The same word can have more than one meaning. A pupil giving a talk to the class is a presenter too. At an awards night, the presenter of a prize is the person who hands it over. Always check which meaning fits the words around it.
fact: A presenter is a person who introduces and hosts a TV or radio programme.
fact: A presenter can also be anyone who gives a talk or presentation to a group.
fact: At an awards show, the presenter of a prize is the person who hands it over.
fact: Phrases you may meet are «TV presenter», «news presenter», «weather presenter» and «guest presenter».
fact: Good presenters speak clearly and look at their audience.
exercise: «A TV weather presenter stands in front of a plain green screen.» What is a presenter in this sentence? | A plant that grows in a green field | A camera that is moved around the room | *A person who hosts or talks on a TV programme | A screen that shows the map
exercise: Maya gives a talk about volcanoes to her class. What does this make her? | A news reader on the radio | *A presenter, because she gives a talk to a group | A prize winner
exercise: «The presenter of the prize was a famous footballer.» What does the presenter do with the prize? | Hides it | Designs it | Wins it | *Hands it over
test: Why are breakfast-show presenters called paid professionals? Clue: «the friendly chat is planned». | Because they never talk to guests | *Because the chat is planned and it is their job | Because they work as unpaid volunteers | Because they are famous singers
test: Which of these is a phrase from the lessons that uses presenter? | Garden helper | Ice cream seller | *Weather presenter | Football coach
exam: «The presenter giggles about a singer's secret heartbreak.» What does presenter mean here? | A person who sells tickets at the door | *A person who hosts a show and talks to the audience | Someone who grows flowers in a garden | A singer who sings on the radio
